&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first occupation of any part of the building by a new occupier, other than a use falling within Class E, an Inclusive Access and Evacuation Management strategy shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Plan shall include details of: &lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
Accessible
WC provision;&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
Accessible
reception arrangements;&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
Hearing
enhancement systems;&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
Accessible
signage and wayfinding;&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
Arrangements
for users with additional access requirements, including refuge facilities,
emergency communication systems, Personal Emergency Evacuation Plans (PEEPs)
and evacuation procedures; &lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
Associated
management and maintenance arrangements.&lt;br&gt;The approved Plan shall be implemented prior
to the first occupation of any part of the building by a use other than a use
falling within Class E, and adhered to thereafter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;Prior to the first occupation of any part of
